*> The six directions of the feature stage by ordinal (docs/protocol/35-worldgen-features-4 section 2.1: DOWN 0, UP 1, NORTH 2, SOUTH 3, WEST 4, EAST 5), as 1-based tables (ordinal + 1):
*> FDR-DX, FDR-DY, FDR-DZ the unit step. The opposite of an ordinal d is d XOR 1 (FDR-OPP(d + 1)).
 01 FDR-STEPS.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE -1.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE -1.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE -1.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 FDR-STEP-TABLE REDEFINES FDR-STEPS.
    05 FDR-STEP OCCURS 6 TIMES.
       10 FDR-DX            BINARY-LONG.
       10 FDR-DY            BINARY-LONG.
       10 FDR-DZ            BINARY-LONG.
 01 FDR-OPPS.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 3.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 2.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 5.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 4.
 01 FDR-OPP-TABLE REDEFINES FDR-OPPS.
    05 FDR-OPP              BINARY-LONG OCCURS 6 TIMES.
